  "Cli.Usage": "Sigwalk file signature inspector\n\nUsage:\n  Sigwalk.exe [options] <file-or-directory> [more paths...]\n\nOptions:\n  -r, --recursive            Scan subfolders recursively (default)\n      --no-recursive         Do not scan subfolders\n  -e, --ext <list>           Extension filter, e.g. exe;dll;sys (empty = all)\n  -j, --concurrency <1-32>   Concurrency\n  -m, --mode <full|signature|hash>\n                             Scan mode\n      --revocation <none|cache|online>\n                             Certificate revocation check\n  -f, --format <csv|json|xlsx>\n                             Export format (requires --output)\n  -c, --content <all|compact>\n                             Export content (requires --output)\n  -o, --output <path>        Export to the specified file\n      --lang <zh|en>         Interface and output language\n      --fail-on-issues       Return exit code 5 when unsigned/invalid/unknown/failed files exist\n  -q, --quiet                Do not print each file result\n  -h, --help                 Show help\n  -V, --version              Show version\n\nExit codes: 0 success; 1 unexpected error; 2 usage error; 3 no files found; 4 export failed; 5 issues found; 130 cancelled.",
